  "narrative": {
    "key_bets": [
      "Spherical tokamak geometry (A=2.3) achieves higher beta to compensate for lower magnetic field (5.25 T on-axis vs 9.2 T for ARC)",
      "REBCO HTS magnet system scales from validated Demo4 (14 TF + 2 PF coils at 11.8 T, 30 K) to full ST-E1 plant scale",
      "Outboard-only liquid lithium blanket achieves TBR = 1.2 despite ~50% solid-angle coverage",
      "ECRH-only (O-mode) auxiliary heating provides sufficient current drive for 15+ minute quasi-steady flat-top operation",
      "WC-FeCr cermet center stack shielding (~32 cm radial depth) protects HTS coils from neutron damage over plant lifetime",
      "Pulsed operation (15+ min pulses with CS re-magnetization dwell) is preferable to steady-state for ST geometry",
      "Burning plasma performance (high Q) achievable to deliver 450–750 MWe net output"
    ],
    "eliminated_costs": [
      "No beryllium required (unlike FLiBe-based blankets such as ARC) — removes one supply chain constraint",
      "Lower REBCO tape performance requirements per unit length due to lower on-axis field (5.25 T vs 9.2 T for ARC)",
      "Reduced magnet mechanical stress from lower field operation",
      "No NBI infrastructure required for flat-top (ECRH-only simplifies plasma physics — no beam-driven rotation, no NBI-first-wall interactions)"
    ],
    "novel_costs": [
      "Thermal energy storage (molten salt buffer) required to smooth pulsed output for grid — capital cost absent from steady-state designs",
      "Center stack WC cermet shielding as separate capital and O&M item — no equivalent in ARC or conventional tokamak",
      "Outboard-only liquid lithium blanket with inert atmosphere handling systems (Li metal chemical reactivity)",
      "Li-6 enrichment to high levels needed to achieve TBR=1.2 with limited blanket coverage",
      "Higher ECRH recirculating power burden due to gyrotron wall-plug efficiency (~50–55%) at multi-tens-of-MW scale"
    ],
    "risks": [
      {
        "description": "Q value, fusion power, and auxiliary heating power all unpublished — no physics anchor for LCOE model; estimates require three unanchored assumptions producing very wide uncertainty bands",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Outboard-only liquid Li blanket at TBR=1.2 is TRL 2–3; no fusion-scale demonstration of liquid Li tritium extraction, Li metal/structural alloy compatibility, or 14 MeV irradiation database",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "WC cermet irradiation performance under 14 MeV fusion neutrons is explicitly uncharacterized; could compromise center stack shielding lifetime and magnet protection",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "No published capital cost estimate or plant study for ST-E1 Rev D — all costs in model are framework defaults with no concept-specific anchoring",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Pulsed operation requires thermal energy storage system that is undimensioned and uncosted; dwell periods reduce effective availability below steady-state designs",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "ECCD current drive efficiency in burning-plasma ST conditions is unvalidated — all existing ECCD data is from non-burning plasmas",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "REBCO tape supply chain (~thousands km/year global capacity) may not scale to fleet deployment; current price ($30–100/kA-m) needs to fall to ~$10/kA-m for commercial viability",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Design has not stabilized — power output increased from 85 MWe (DPP 2024) to 450–750 MWe (DPP 2025 Rev D), indicating active redesign and uncertain final design point",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Tritium supply constraint shared across D-T concepts — ~25–30 kg global inventory declining as CANDU reactors retire; outboard-only blanket more sensitive to local coverage gaps",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Capacity factor target unpublished; pulsed operation with CS re-magnetization dwell may push toward lower end of 75–90% D-T MCF range",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Component replacement schedules (blanket, divertor, center stack) undisclosed — affects availability and O&M cost estimates",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ]
  },
